Package: brain
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Matthew Hagrelius <matthew@hagreli.us>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/mhagrelius/brain
Description: A Markdown notebook that leaves your notes as files
 Brain is a note-taking app for GNOME whose notes are ordinary Markdown files
 in a folder you choose. Delete Brain and they are untouched; put the folder in
 git and you have history; open it in any other editor and it reads the same.
 .
 The editor styles Markdown as you write it and hides the syntax characters
 everywhere except the block you are working in, so a note reads as prose while
 staying plain text on disk.
 .
 It adds [[wikilinks]] with completion and backlinks, renames that repoint every
 link pointing at a note, nested tags from both inline #tags and frontmatter,
 attachments you drop or paste with images shown in the note, and search across
 titles or the full text of every note.
 .
 No account, no sync, no plugins.
